WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:06.640
The Goffard Theater is silent, save for the
occasional shifting of your fellow Foundation

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:07.640
researcher.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.849
The two of you are alone, and you’ve been
tasked with transcribing the performances

00:00:11.849 --> 00:00:14.990
of SCP-6373.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:19.539
You read the file, understood the briefing,
and you even told yourself that you’re prepared

00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:24.550
to witness whatever obscene show is about
to commence, but you’ve never experienced

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:28.179
SCP-6373 firsthand.

00:00:28.179 --> 00:00:33.040
This is your first time, filling in for another
researcher who got herself injured during

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.930
one of the performances.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:37.140
You hope it wasn’t anything serious.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:40.690
The lights flash, pointing to the main stage.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:43.720
The smell of rot is almost overwhelming now.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:47.820
You swear you see a family of rats scurry
under your front row seats.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.980
The curtains fly open, revealing…

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.079
nothing.

00:00:52.079 --> 00:00:56.470
You expect someone to come out from behind
the curtain, but the stage is barren.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:01:01.770
Suddenly, a loud, creaking noise is heard
from above, and four broken, poorly painted,

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:05.400
and utterly deranged looking puppets drop
from the ceiling.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:11.219
Their strings are slightly visible, and their
movements fluctuate between quick, jerky motions

00:01:11.219 --> 00:01:13.420
and slow, weighty ones.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:19.219
The one with the long nose starts talking
in a high-pitched, lofty voice, asking the

00:01:19.219 --> 00:01:22.439
desolate audience if they’re ready for the
show.

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:26.289
You start to wonder when things are going
to kick in and really cement this anomaly’s

00:01:26.289 --> 00:01:29.340
status as a terrifying SCP object.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:32.829
For the first five minutes, the show isn’t
too bad.

00:01:32.829 --> 00:01:37.330
The puppets sing and dance a bit creepy, but
they’re not doing anything wrong.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:42.889
At least, that’s what you think until the
long-nosed one brandishes a baseball bat and

00:01:42.889 --> 00:01:49.259
savagely smashes the smaller, round one to
a pulp, splattering guts and insides all over

00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:50.259
the theater.

00:01:50.259 --> 00:01:52.670
And it only gets worse from there.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:02:00.310
Welcome to the Goffard Theater, the home of
SCP-6373, codenamed by those researching it

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:03.289
as “Stage Blight”.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:08.979
SCP-6373 refers to a collection of four papier-mâché
puppets, each standing around one meter in

00:02:08.979 --> 00:02:12.390
height and complete with attached strings.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:15.720
These puppets constantly emit a rotting, disgusting
stench.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:20.010
Though the Foundation has come to the conclusion
that this smell is entirely non-anomalous.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:28.140
SCP-6373 gain their anomalous properties at
around 6 PM each day, as long as they’re

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:34.120
positioned inside the Goffard Theater, a building
located in the city of Reading, Pennsylvania,

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.340
which is where the Foundation has chosen to
contain the four objects.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:44.960
If SCP-6373 aren’t inside the Goffard Theater,
they instead start decomposing, rotting and

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:48.310
breaking down into a stinky, smelly mess of
puppet-materials.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:55.010
So, what happens when SCP-6373 take on their
anomalous properties?

00:02:55.010 --> 00:03:00.880
The puppets gain sentience, mobility, and
limited intelligence, though attempts to communicate

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:05.730
with SCP-6373 outside of their performances
have failed.

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:08.820
Sorry, no puppet interview logs for today.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:13.930
They then proceed to the main stage of the
Goffard Theater, and put on a puppet show!

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:17.599
Wow, a whole performance, isn’t that sweet?

00:03:17.599 --> 00:03:25.180
Not really, SCP-6373’s performances are
notoriously brutal, unpredictable, and terrifying.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:29.080
So much so that the Foundation has offered
counseling services to the poor personnel

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:30.730
forced to watch them.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:35.310
That’s right, there must be at least one
observing personnel in the Goffard Theater

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:42.640
to witness SCP-6373’s performance, or else
the puppets drop to the floor and start decomposing

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:43.640
again.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:48.880
Following their performance, the puppets lose
all sentience until 6 PM on the next day,

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:50.690
when the process repeats.

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:55.430
But let’s talk about SCP-6373 themselves.

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:58.030
These puppets have a lot of character.

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:05.180
You have Pierre, SCP-6373-1, the main character
of the performances, who just loves to verbally

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:09.200
and physically abuse his fellow wooden companions.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:16.400
Glouton, SCP-6373-2, is a large, disembodied
head with a gaping mouth, who speaks only

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:21.310
in single-word statements and deep, guttural
moans.

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:27.570
SCP-6373-3 is a tiny, grey, round ball known
as “Ame”, who remains entirely silent

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:33.290
throughout the performances, despite being
the puppet abused by the others the most frequently.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:40.620
The puppet, SCP-6373-4, Jacque, is a long-necked
clown who serves as the group’s comedic

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:41.620
relief.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:46.320
But before we delve into the horrific performances
put on by these entities, let’s talk about

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:47.690
the Goffard Theater.

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:53.340
The theater was opened in 1860 by french immigrant
Timothee Goffard for the purposes of putting

00:04:53.340 --> 00:05:01.780
on stage plays, musical performances, and
in-house puppet shows that featured SCP-6373.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:06.590
The puppets were designed by Goffard himself,
and were massively profitable and popular

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:07.740
with Reading’s children.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:13.520
While it’s not known if SCP-6373 possessed
their anomalous properties during the original

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:18.710
run of performances, the Foundation doesn’t
believe they did, and they were otherwise

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:21.870
ordinary puppets, controlled by puppeteers.

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:25.540
Unfortunately, the Goffard Theater was not
built to last.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:31.720
In 1884, it closed its doors after a legal
battle between Goffard and his wife, Cynthia

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:33.880
raged through the courts.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:38.730
Cynthia was accused of stealing money from
the theater, to which she defended herself,

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:43.380
saying that Timothee was not only unfaithful
in their marriage, but also physically and

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.139
verbally abusive to her.

00:05:45.139 --> 00:05:50.940
The lawsuit ended in a divorce, and an ominously
worded letter written to Cynthia by Timothee.

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:56.870
“… I write to you in poor health, and
all joy sapped from my life.

00:05:56.870 --> 00:06:01.100
May misfortune follow you until the end of
your days.

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:08.660
I will not construct again that which I had
spent two decades of my life working towards.

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:15.470
I can only thank God’s grace that the building
has remained vacant, as I could not bear to

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:17.030
see it owned by another man.

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:21.960
I want to perform again, and see the children
smile.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:24.980
My happiness was so linked to theirs.”

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:28.990
A week later, Timothee Goffard disappeared
entirely.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:33.410
Four months later, Cynthia Goffard supposedly
died of natural causes.

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:39.980
In 1887, Foundation precursor organization,
the American Secure Containment Initiative,

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:47.870
or ASCI for short, discovered SCP-6373 inside
the theater and documented its anomalous properties

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:50.010
shortly after.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:56.760
SCP-6373 had a captive audience, and containment
persisted long after the ASCI had assimilated

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:59.480
into the SCP Foundation.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:05.370
And now we can get to the part you’ve all
been waiting for, the performances themselves.

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:11.260
The Foundation has kept a log of all of SCP-6373’s
performances, but here are some of the most

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:13.350
notable ones.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:19.980
SCP-6373’s first performance, in 1887, involved
lighting fixtures around the theater collectively

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:25.960
powering on several minutes before the show,
as well as a slight piano accompaniment, originating

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:27.790
from an unknown source.

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:30.010
The contents of the show were simple.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:34.960
Pierre rescued a princess, a costumed Jacque,
from a dragon, played by Glouton.

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:38.430
Researchers noted several moments when one
of the puppets had difficulty maintaining

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:43.180
posture and moving, often taking multiple
attempts to lift limbs.

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:46.080
These moments increased in frequency over
time.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:50.449
In 1895, the puppets performed a show about
a bank robbery gone wrong.

00:07:50.449 --> 00:07:54.699
Pierre decided that Ame was the one who alerted
the police about their crime, and spent the

00:07:54.699 --> 00:08:00.150
rest of the performance berating and abusing
the small puppet, specifically for “betraying

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:04.889
its trust and breaking the bond they had shared
after years of working together”, as Pierre

00:08:04.889 --> 00:08:05.889
put it.

00:08:05.889 --> 00:08:09.889
The puppets use Ame as a soccer-ball, but
their game quickly devolves into a contest

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:12.759
of trying to see who can kick it the hardest.

00:08:12.759 --> 00:08:16.759
Ame is noted to be silently crying throughout
all of this.

00:08:16.759 --> 00:08:21.729
In 1916, the puppets put on a World War I
period piece, taking place on a farm owned

00:08:21.729 --> 00:08:24.550
by husband Pierre and his wife, Ame.

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:29.550
Pierre, upset that his crops were destroyed
by the ongoing war, asks Ame for support,

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:34.960
but the puppet remains silent, even as Pierre’s
cries grow louder and more frantic.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:39.610
Pierre then shifts the blame of the crop’s
destruction from the war to Ame itself.

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:43.510
He states that Ame will never be “let out”
of the house again.

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:46.930
Sounds of war and human suffering were heard
throughout.

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:52.900
In 1922, the puppets repeated their first
performance, about the princess and the castle.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:57.420
Except this time, the puppets sounded a lot
angrier in their dialogue delivery, and their

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:01.850
movements are described as frantic bursts
in between moments where they do nothing but

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:03.250
hang limp.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:07.470
Pierre yells at Glouton for an apparently
poor performance as the Princess, and when

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:13.570
the puppet pretends to play dead, Pierre specifically
states that’s “not what being dead feels

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:14.570
like”.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:19.170
In 1938, the puppets attempted to perform
a comedy routine, but quickly found out that

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:23.880
their slow, unsynchronized movements were
causing problems with the pacing and effectiveness

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:24.990
of their act.

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:30.040
Pierre became frustrated, and brandished a
prop fire hose, which he sprayed at the fellow

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:33.112
puppets, causing them to scream as their paint
ran off and chipped.

00:09:33.112 --> 00:09:37.710
The screams heard throughout the theater were
notably feminine.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:43.160
In 1952, Pierre performed a piano duet with
Jacque, who was unable to sit still or keep

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:44.830
quiet during the act.

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:49.790
The annoyed Pierre proceeded to savagely slam
Jacque’s head into the piano until it was

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:53.160
dented, and his jaw was detached completely.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:57.800
The Jacque puppet began leaking a disgusting
yellow fluid from its mouth.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:02.700
Pierre fetched Ame and forced the tiny puppet
to sit in the fluid, all while Jacque writhed

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:03.700
in pain.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:07.580
While the damage sustained by the puppets
during each performance was healed and restored

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:13.630
by the next day through anomalous means, Jacque’s
jaw was never fixed, and he continued to seep

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:17.170
fluid for the duration of the anomaly’s
containment.

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:21.130
1958’s performance was only two minutes
in length, and featured Pierre attempting

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:22.890
to teach an art class.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:27.960
Glouton’s canvas displayed the words “OPEN
INSIDE”, which for some reason angered Pierre

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:31.970
enough to end the performance entirely and
lead the puppets offstage.

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:37.910
For the next 24 hours, an unidentified male
voice screamed and swore from behind the stage’s

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:41.060
curtain, throwing objects and punching walls.

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:47.050
The source was not discerned, and no SCP-6373
instances could be found within the theater

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:53.640
until the next day at 6 PM, when they reemerged
from the back and performed as usual.

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:57.350
This 1963 performance was particularly bizarre.

00:10:57.350 --> 00:11:02.589
Pierre took the stage by himself, and proceeded
to deliver a eulogy for Timothee Goffard in

00:11:02.589 --> 00:11:04.800
the voice of an unidentified woman.

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:08.940
Strangely, the Foundation discovered that
a funeral service was not held for Goffard.

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:13.700
In 1971, the puppet’s performances became
a lot more lifeless.

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:17.570
Their voices became monotone and their movements
were slower.

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:23.000
Oftentimes, a puppet would have to hit itself
in order to restore fluid motion to its limbs.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:26.420
This would continue in all future performances.

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:33.770
In 1973, SCP-6373 performed a sitcom skit,
in which Pierre and his two “sons”, played

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:37.700
by Jacque and Glouton, took turns beating
and breaking Ame.

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:42.220
This trend of physical abuse towards Ame would
increase in frequency as time went on, like

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:48.330
in this four hour 1976 performance that consisted
of the silhouettes of the puppets from behind

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:53.290
the stage torturing the poor thing, all while
Ame silently took it.

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:57.190
All the while, Pierre told Ame that it was
the sole reason the puppets were in their

00:11:57.190 --> 00:12:01.750
current situation, and why they were unable
to move forward.

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:06.830
In 1979, the Goffard Theater’s structural
integrity was observed to be failing.

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:10.850
Masses of rats, termites, and fungi were discovered
throughout the building.

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:15.170
Similarly, the performances themselves became
even more disturbing.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:19.410
One involved the puppets reenacting the life
story of Timothee Goffard, but refused to

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:21.959
acknowledge or mention his wife Cynthia.

00:12:21.959 --> 00:12:27.630
Instead, they claimed he died alone and miserable,
without ever experiencing love.

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:31.890
The performance ended with Pierre smashing
its head against the floor and knocking it

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:36.649
off, unleashing a swarm of blow fly larvae
that Foundation was unable to remove from

00:12:36.649 --> 00:12:37.649
the theater.

00:12:37.649 --> 00:12:43.040
In 1983, the puppets performed a skit in which
they held a funeral for Ame.

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:48.040
After exploring a variety of possible afterlifes
from various religions, the puppets were understandably

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:52.670
confused about which one was “correct”,
and how they could achieve salvation.

00:12:52.670 --> 00:12:57.010
Then, Jacque had an epiphany, exclaiming:
“I know the answer!

00:12:57.010 --> 00:12:58.240
We're all dead!

00:12:58.240 --> 00:13:00.490
This is the only afterlife there is!”.

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:03.790
The puppets then went limp, and stayed that
way for a week.

00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:08.430
By 1984, the puppets put almost zero effort
into their performances.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:13.010
One involved them openly fantasizing about
injuring the audience members, and ended with

00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:17.580
the puppets picking a poor Foundation researcher
from the audience as a “volunteer” and

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:21.090
snapping her arm, all while laughing.

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:25.150
Another had the puppets stating the full names,
birthdays, and death dates of every patron

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:30.980
of the Goffard theater from its opening to
the present, and this included the Foundation

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:32.649
researchers watching.

00:13:32.649 --> 00:13:37.510
SCP-6373’s movements were awkward and slow,
their speech slurred.

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:40.660
It was clear that the puppets were on their
last limb.

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:46.240
In 1985, every performance had degenerated
to a frenzy of self-harm carried out by the

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:52.870
puppet, devoid of any stage lighting and accompanied
by a noisey, barely harmonious musical accompaniment.

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:56.269
Feminine screams and male laughter is heard
throughout.

00:13:56.269 --> 00:14:00.769
But things got even worse throughout the year,
as performances further degraded to periods

00:14:00.769 --> 00:14:06.180
of sitting or standing still and incoherent
rambling while facing the audience.

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:12.380
The performances were entirely indecipherable,
and all dialogue consisted of grunting, moaning,

00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:14.130
screaming, and weeping.

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:20.899
On June 6th, 1985, SCP-6373 put on another
performance.

00:14:20.899 --> 00:14:27.120
The puppets stood side by side for 18 minutes
before bowing and falling to the ground.

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:29.970
No lights or music was heard.

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:35.740
Following this performance, the puppets began
to decay, shedding their papier-mache exteriors.

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:39.579
When this was complete, the insides of the
puppets were revealed to be composed of human

00:14:39.579 --> 00:14:41.420
remains and organs.

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:47.640
Pierre contained a brain, Jacque a heart,
Glouton a mass of skin and tissue, and Ame

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:48.750
was empty.

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:53.560
All of this material had been cut cleanly
and sourced from a single individual.

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:57.681
When the Foundation unrolled the skin tissue
contained inside the Glouton puppet, there

00:14:57.681 --> 00:15:05.550
was no doubt about which individual it resembled
- Cynthia Cordier, the wife of Timothee Goffard.

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:11.000
The object was reclassified as neutralized,
and no further performances or anomalous activity

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:16.070
relating to SCP-6373 was ever observed.

00:15:16.070 --> 00:15:22.800
Now go check out “SCP-701 - The Hanged King's
Tragedy” and “SCP-5049 - Demon Dan's Discount

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:27.980
Homunculus Depot” for more SCPs that blur
the line between entertainment and terror!

